  "id": "field-of-consciousness",
  "term": "field of consciousness",
  "definition": "Field of consciousness is the whole contents of awareness present at one moment, understood as if spread out like a visual field. In this historical usage, attention is treated as focusing on one part of that field, and the field may become broader or narrower depending on the person and on conditions such as attention, health, or disorder.",
